course: dictionary
lesson: 1434
title: The carpel: the female part of a flower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A flower is a set of parts, and each part has a job. The carpel is the female part of a flower, in the middle, where seeds are made. «A flower has petals, stamens that make pollen and a carpel in the middle holding tiny ovules, which become seeds once pollen reaches the carpel.»
explain: The carpel has three parts: the stigma, which is the sticky top that catches pollen; the style, which is the stalk; and the ovary, which is the bottom part with ovules inside.
explain: The text gives you a clue. «Its job is to make seeds, and for that, pollen from the stamens must reach the carpel in the middle.» If pollen must reach the carpel to make seeds, the carpel must be where seeds are made. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: A carpel is the female part of a flower, where seeds are made.
fact: The stigma is the sticky top of the carpel, and it catches pollen.
fact: The style is the stalk of the carpel.
fact: The ovary is the bottom part of the carpel, with ovules inside that become seeds.
fact: After pollination, the ovary can grow into the fruit. Some flowers have one carpel, and others have many, like a buttercup or a strawberry.
exercise: «A flower has petals, stamens that make pollen and a carpel in the middle.» What is the carpel? | The green leaves under the flower | The coloured petals that attract insects | The male part, which makes pollen | *The female part of the flower, where seeds are made
exercise: Which part of the carpel is the sticky top that catches pollen? | The style | The petal | The ovary | *The stigma
exercise: «Pollen from the stamens must reach the carpel, and that delivery is pollination.» What is the name for pollen reaching the carpel? | Photosynthesis | Germination | *Pollination | Fertilisation
test: Which part of the carpel grows into the fruit after pollination? | *The ovary | The style | The stamen | The stigma
test: Which part of the carpel is the stalk? | The stigma | The ovary | *The style | The sepal
exam: Pollen from a stamen lands on the sticky top of a carpel, and seeds start to form. Which part of the carpel holds the ovules that become seeds? | The filament | *The ovary | The stigma | The style
